<title>USA: U.S. producers hold meat safety symposium in Japan.</title>
<headline>U.S. producers hold meat safety symposium in Japan.</headline>
<dateline>DENVER 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>A U.S. delegation will take part on Monday in a food safety symposium in Japan to assure consumers there that American meat is safe and wholesome, the U.S. Meat Export Federation said on Friday.</p>
<p>The symposium, sponsored by the federation, will involve executives from Japanese retail, foodservice and distribution sectors, the Denver-based meat export group said.</p>
<p>The trip is in response to growing concerns about the safety of imported meat into the region, the group said.</p>
</text>
